  "finding_on_247ms_discrepancy": "In run_50_real_questions_benchmark.py (line 299), the author did NOT run parallel threads or the Cross-Encoder reranker; instead, the script computed: t_acamind_ret_ms = max(t_dense_ret_ms, t_bm25_ret_ms) + t_fusion_ms + (0.08 if dcsr_skipped else 185.0). Because t_dense_ret_ms had P50 = 65.1 ms and 40/50 queries had dcsr_skipped=False, adding the hardcoded 185.0 ms constant produced 62.2 + 185.0 = 247.2 ms! In real execution measured here, parallel HNSW+GIN takes ~max(HNSW, GIN) + thread/connection overhead, whereas real Cross-Encoder reranking on CPU takes far longer than 185 ms."
